This project uses a modular license structure based on Android IPC process isolation:

1. `app/` Module:
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (Apache-2.0). See app/LICENSE for details.

2. `MenthaAR/` Engine Module:
   Derived from ORB-SLAM2 and released under the GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPLv3). See MenthaAR/LICENSE for details.

3. `MenthaAR-ipc/` Interface Module:
   Dual-licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (Apache-2.0) or the GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPLv3).
   The recipient may choose either license. See MenthaAR-ipc/LICENSE, MenthaAR-ipc/LICENSE-APACHE-2.0 and
   MenthaAR-ipc/LICENSE-GPL-3.0 for details. When this module is used under Apache-2.0, only the Apache-2.0
   terms apply to it and no GPLv3 obligation is triggered by that module itself.

4. Inter-Process Communication (IPC):
   The `app` module and `MenthaAR` engine run in separate OS processes and communicate strictly via Binder IPC and SharedMemory (Ashmem/memfd), preserving license boundaries. The `app` module depends on `MenthaAR-ipc` at compile time only and packages the GPLv3 engine as a runtime-only artifact.

Please see Dependencies.md for a list of all included code and library dependencies that are not the property of the authors of ORB-SLAM2.

For a closed-source version of ORB-SLAM2 for commercial purposes, please contact the original authors.

Authors' Statement on AI Model Training (non-binding)

The authors state a preference that this software not be used, in whole or in
part, for training, fine-tuning or evaluating proprietary or closed-source
artificial intelligence models, and invite users who build open-source models
with it to keep their resulting works open as well.

This statement is a declaration of intent only. It is not a license condition:
it does not add any restriction to, or remove any right granted by, the GNU
General Public License v3.0 or the Apache License 2.0, and it creates no
obligation for any recipient. Rights and obligations for each module are
governed exclusively by the applicable license texts listed above: app/LICENSE,
MenthaAR-ipc/LICENSE and MenthaAR/LICENSE.

If you use ORB-SLAM in academic work, please cite the most relevant publication associated with the project by visiting:
https://github.com/raulmur/ORB_SLAM2
